[Music]  food companies work hard to ensure their  products are safe for allergic consumers  they often use the same production line  for different products or they share  facilities with other companies  so it's essential that they test for the  unintentional presence of food allergens  even after rigorous cleaning  these tests and their results can vary  considerably between laboratories  therefore companies take the extra  precaution of including warnings on  labels indicating that products may  contain traces of other allergenic  ingredients  could we help companies to avoid  overusing these warnings on labels by  increasing their confidence in allergen  tests and in turn give allergic  consumers more choice in the future  we have been working on a system to test  and produce reliable and comparable data  across thousands of laboratories  we started by developing a reference  method to accurately assess the total  content of milk protein in a cookie with  the same protocol for all manufacturers  we would guarantee comparable results  we chose milk because allergy to cow's  milk is still one of the most common  food allergies in early childhood and  can persist through adult life  we are developing the world's first  certified reference material for the  detection of total milk protein in  processed food  when released this certified reference  material will help food companies and  official control laboratories to  calibrate their instruments  and with better calibration they will  obtain more precise measurements with  more certainty about the data gathered  and to make our efforts known we  establish the european network of food  allergen detection laboratories which  will share the knowledge across all eu  member states  the european commissioner for health and  food safety has referred our work to the  european parliament as an important  contribution  it will help curb the proliferation of  labels  while giving allergic consumers more  choices in full confidence  every day the joint research center  works to ensure that the data produced  across europe is comparable  helping consumers to be confident in the  well-informed choices they make find out  more on our website

